 # Working notes: b9ba0104b1b6
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## 2026-10-24 constructive crop-to-content repair
+
+### Observed defects
+
+- The imported 2.1.0 source omitted the canonical `RULE_HASH`, advertised shape
+  controls that were not honestly observable, and made difficulty effectively
+  byte-identical.
+- Ordinary samples forced all four content-box corners. That let a
+  corner-anchored crop shortcut fit the generated support even though the
+  canonical rule is the bounding box of *all* nonzero cells.
+- The task had no task-local regression tests or reusable adversarial probe.
+
+### Repair
+
+- Replaced the sampler with deterministic version 3.0.0 and pinned
+  `RULE_HASH = "9de647fc93bf"`. Generation is constructive rather than
+  retry/fallback-based.
+- Public axes are exact and observable: canvas 10..30, content box 3..6,
+  foreground color 1..9, and three ordinary textures. Unknown keys, invalid
+  numeric types, negative indexes, and unsupported difficulties fail loudly.
+- Every three consecutive ordinary examples cycle through:
+  1. `noncorner_cross`: all four bbox sides matter while every corner is zero;
+  2. `disconnected_extents`: no single component determines the global bbox;
+  3. `dense_hole`: the crop must preserve interior background.
+- All ordinary examples have positive padding on every outer side. Explicit
+  `fills_grid` and `single_cell` degenerates remain diagnostic-only.
+- Default profiles preserve the three canonical dimension/color profiles first,
+  broaden to a 30x30 case, and give medium/hard larger average canvases while
+  retaining sparse canonical-profile support in every band.
+- Added `rule_mirror`, strict validation, override observation, lesson-level
+  rival checks, focused regressions, and reusable
+  `workspace/adversarial_review.py`.
+
+### Test-first evidence
+
+- Retained failing runs for the original contract, output diversity, dead
+  difficulty, missing profile-floor support, and the new audit tool under
+  `checks/b9ba0104b1b6-*-red.log`.
+- Final focused suite: 23/23 passed.
+- Protected adversarial audit: 36/36 three-demonstration windows passed over
+  seeds 0/17/97, starts 0/1/2, and default/easy/medium/hard; 70 distinct inputs
+  were executed through protected Racket, producing 47 distinct outputs. All
+  four declared rivals were refuted, and every difficulty band retained
+  canonical-profile support.
+- Final native battery: 12/12 stages green (`lint`, `selfcheck`, `rule_smoke`,
+  `defect_lint`, `dist_gate`, `profile_floor`, `semantic_gate`, `diversity`,
+  `override`, `grammar`, `racket_lint`, `authority_sync`).
+- Final source SHA-256:
+  `4033712b9da2fef99bada3be410fb3318bbf10f92567948aa98d59397cc64458`.
+
+### Limits and handoff
+
+The adversarial claim is bounded to the four declared rivals and sampled
+three-example windows; it is not universal identifiability. This task was
+catalog-unapproved in the assignment. The repair is a source-bound proposal for
+owner-checked integration and does not grant approval or training admission.
+Imported associated notes remain in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
